---
import Layout from '@layouts/default.astro';
import EditorialImage from '@components/EditorialImage.astro';
import ContactPanel from '@components/ContactPanel.astro';
import profile from '@assets/images/profile.webp';
import skyline from '@assets/images/new-york-brooklyn-bridge.webp';
---

<Layout
  title="About Andrew Noblet"
  description="Meet Andrew Noblet, a New York-based software engineer working on design, web development, and accessible digital experiences."
>
  <div class="editorial-page">
    <section class="editorial-hero">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Hello, I’m Andrew</p><h1>
          Curious by nature.<br />Practical by choice.
        </h1><p>
          I’m Andrew, a software engineer based in Tarrytown, New York. I work
          on websites, interfaces, and the systems behind them, with an interest
          in making technology easier to understand and use.
        </p><div class="editorial-actions">
          <a class="editorial-button" href="/portfolio/professional"
            >Explore my work →</a
          ><a href="/contact">Let’s talk →</a>
        </div>
      </div><figure>
        <EditorialImage src={profile} alt="Andrew Noblet" priority />
      </figure>
    </section>
    <section class="editorial-section editorial-split">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">01 / How I work</p><h2>
          Less noise.<br />More meaning.
        </h2>
      </div><div class="editorial-prose">
        <p>
          I like to understand the problem before adding complexity. Who is
          using the website? What are they trying to do? Which parts need to
          work together? Those questions guide choices about content, layout,
          and implementation.
        </p><p>
          My work includes online learning, e-commerce, and business websites. I
          use tools such as Astro, Lit, JavaScript, and TypeScript, choosing an
          approach around the project rather than starting with a framework.
        </p><p>
          You work directly with me. We define the scope, make room for
          feedback, and keep practical details such as handoff and maintenance
          part of the conversation.
        </p><a href="/services">See how I can help →</a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="editorial-section editorial-split">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">02 / Beyond the screen</p><h2>
          From Santiago to New York.
        </h2><EditorialImage
          src={skyline}
          alt="Brooklyn Bridge and Manhattan at dusk"
        />
      </div><div class="editorial-prose">
        <p>
          I was born in Santiago, Chile, and have lived in Puerto Rico, Ohio,
          and New York. My interests range from skateboarding, snowboarding, and
          biking to guitar, 3D printing, and home automation.
        </p><p>
          Eastern philosophy and Greek mythology are recurring interests. I
          value curiosity, preparation, and simplicity in both my work and daily
          life.
        </p><details>
          <summary>Early projects and interests</summary><div
            class="editorial-prose"
          >
            <p>
              I built my first website at 13 and explored PHP, php-nuke,
              Dreamweaver, and ColdFusion. Building a water-cooled computer also
              taught me a practical lesson about preparation and testing.
            </p><p>
              At 14, I petitioned my town for a skatepark. That experience stays
              with me as an example of turning an idea into something useful
              through persistence and communication.
            </p><p>
              Today I still enjoy projects that connect ideas to physical
              things, whether that is a 3D-printed object, a smart-home
              automation, or learning a new piece of music.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details><a href="https://github.com/anoblet"
          >Find my work on GitHub →</a
        >
      </div>
    </section>
    <ContactPanel title="Have something in mind?" />
  </div>
</Layout>
